{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1296721-most-populous-tribe-by-state","id":1296721,"title":"Most populous Tribe by State","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-14T09:25:36-07:00","id":1296721,"title":"Most populous Tribe by State","content":"Thinking about if I ever ran another WtA chronicle and how the tribal demographics of my state of Texas would be I started to wonder what others think would be most populous in their state. I'll start and if this sounds interesting chime in. This isn't based on canon but as an interpretation of how I see my home state being represented most accurately. If you're not an American you could still list your interpretation but it probably is more easily defined since the tribes have fairly well defined canon examples of European strongholds.<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia: This tribe would be focused around the largely liberal city and capitol of the state Austin where they could attempt to influence mortal politics in the favor of green and humanitarian initiatives.<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers: With the third highest homeless numbers via the US Interagency Council on Homelessness in the nation the Gnawers would be present in the largest cities Houston, DFW, and Austin and with some hillfolk clans spread throughout the state.<br /> <br /> Get of Fenris: A large number of German immigrants back in the 1800's the Get would have found a number of caerns to claim from the Uktena and have established themselves as one of the dominant tribes of the state.<br /> <br /> Glass Walkers: With Texas being well known for its high technology focus second only to California it has a large presence of Glass Walkers in the highly modern cities of Houston and Dallas.<br /> <br /> Uktena: A traditional stronghold of the Tribe they have lost many caerns in the centuries since the arrival of the Europeans but they remain a significant presence along the Gulf of Mexico and the few pockets of Native American communities in the state.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Hecata are a sect not a clan.","edited":{"userid":24211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24211-frontline989","user":"Frontline989","date":". 03-15-2019, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24211-frontline989","name":"Frontline989","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T10:40:17-07:00","id":1296739,"title":"","content":"Pennsylvania... so a bit of everyone!<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers - between PA's historical connections to the history of the country that the Gnawers really dig, not great homeless and poverty statistics, and being the northern extent of the Appalachians... we'd have plenty of them around.<br /> <br /> Get of Fenris - it's PA, we've got a lot of strong German roots and all that (over 1/4 of the white population here is of German descent). Plus we're kind of notoriously up for a fight.<br /> <br /> Fianna - Oh, right the second largest ethnic group among white people here is the Irish, and some overlap with the Gnawers on distributions. Did I mention PA's reputation for being passionate and fighty sports fans?<br /> <br /> Black Furies - While not common in general across the state, the larger cities tend to have enough Greek population that you'd expect the Furies to be around doing their thing. <br /> <br /> Children of Gaia and Glass Walkers: No special reason for them to be here in general, but PA has plenty of major cities to draw them in with. The Quakers are probably a group the CoGs love too.<br /> <br /> Shadow Lords - PA's German population and relative political power should mean we'd have a good number of them in the mix as well.<br /> <br /> Silver Fangs - Definitely not state-wide, but the Philly area has a lot of old money by US standards. Grace Kelly becoming actual royalty makes a surprising amount of sense as a kin of House Wyrmfoe marrying into a more traditional royal family when you look at the Philly Kelly family history.<br /> <br /> Uktena - Extremely specific to the Philly area, PA was more Croatoan before the European settlement and there's no formally recognized reservations in PA (though many of the tribes that used to live here are still around). IIRC about a decade ago though, a couple willed their land back to the Lenape giving them their first official holding in their traditional home territory in centuries; a great reason for a few Uktena to relocate and try to fix everything that's been mucked up in the meantime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T13:17:27-07:00","id":1296780,"title":"","content":"Denial-The Traditional domain of the SIlver Fangs but with solid showings from all the other tribes especially the Red Talons","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T15:44:15-07:00","id":1296810,"title":"","content":"I live in eastern Tennessee, so canonically, it's whatever Rage Across Appalachia said. Though, personally, I go with the Fianna (mostly of Scots-Irish decent) being one of the largest, along with Bone Gnawer Hillfolk (as well as a scattering of Road Warders, Rat Finks, Hood, and Frankweilers), and Get of Fenris. Then there are Uktena of both Cherokee and African American lineage. Interestingly, Nashville has the largest population of Kurds in the United States. Which could conceivably include Silent Striders, Children of Gaia, Black Furies, Silver Fangs (Wise Heart), and Uktena. While efforts were made to reintroduce red wolves into Tennessee, results were mixed. One major problem was coyotes spreading into the region and cross breeding with them. This is probably a set back for the Red Talons (and very possibly causing those in the region to go on a violent culling of coyotes and a conflict with Nuwisha). One the other hand, cougars are also making a comeback in the region, which is good for the Pumonica. Also black bears, and ravens. No crocodilians, but a nice variety of venomous snakes and spiders. <br /> <br /> I'm still kind of amazed that there was never a Rage Across Alaska book. Aside from the fact that it's a great setting for the game (massive wilderness, a large Native population, and a lot of oil, mining, timber and fishing industry), White Wolf was really big on the Alaskan wolf hunting cause back in the early 90s. And it would've been cool to see a setting where the Wendigo and Red Talons are two of the most populous tribes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T02:52:40-07:00","id":1296936,"title":"","content":"Not USA, but I figure if anyone want to involve Finland in the mix, having uusimaa statted out could help.<br /> <br /> Get of Fenris: I mean, Finland is one of their tribal countries, so obviously. Though in the very south of Uusimaa, they would mostly hang out in the woods of Espoo and so on. Assume them being around but not actually in 'power' as it were.<br /> <br /> Glass Walkers: At least in Helsinki, there is not only a lot of technological development, but a lot of support for it. So there would be a large GW presence in the capital.<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers: In a bit of a pickle, though still numerous. Finland has what is often called as a nanny state, so most of the time people are well cared for. We have homeless people and obviously the system is not perfect. However, I think Gnawers might actually reject the system as EXTREMELY Weavery.<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia: These guys actually are canonical in Finland, so I'd say they do their part in enforcing a more green Uusimaa.<br /> <br /> Black Furies: Women are in a much better position in Finland than in many other countries, so I bet some Furies find their home here.<br /> <br /> Shadow Lords, Silent Striders and Fera: With the influx of immigrants, plus eastern europeans coming here, these guys have grown in numbers.<br /> <br /> Some notes:<br /> <br /> -Being green is EXTREMELY in vogue. People will literally separate their trash to general, paper, cardboard,glass,metal and plastic. Caring for the enviroment is similarly encouraged.<br /> <br /> -Wolves are highly politicized issue. A program about Finland's threastened wildlife got death threats a-plenty when it dealt with wolves.<br /> <br /> -Native Fera would be guralh(VERY respected), corax and ratkin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 03-15-2019, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T10:01:04-07:00","id":1297014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frontline989</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1296721-most-populous-tribe-by-state#post1296721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking about if I ever ran another WtA chronicle and how the tribal demographics of my state of Texas would be I started to wonder what others think would be most populous in their state. I'll start and if this sounds interesting chime in. This isn't based on canon but as an interpretation of how I see my home state being represented most accurately. If you're not an American you could still list your interpretation but it probably is more easily defined since the tribes have fairly well defined canon examples of European strongholds.<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia: This tribe would be focused around the largely liberal city and capitol of the state Austin where they could attempt to influence mortal politics in the favor of green and humanitarian initiatives.<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers: With the third highest homeless numbers via the US Interagency Council on Homelessness in the nation the Gnawers would be present in the largest cities Houston, DFW, and Austin and with some hillfolk clans spread throughout the state.<br /> <br /> Get of Fenris: A large number of German immigrants back in the 1800's the Get would have found a number of caerns to claim from the Uktena and have established themselves as one of the dominant tribes of the state.<br /> <br /> Glass Walkers: With Texas being well known for its high technology focus second only to California it has a large presence of Glass Walkers in the highly modern cities of Houston and Dallas.<br /> <br /> Uktena: A traditional stronghold of the Tribe they have lost many caerns in the centuries since the arrival of the Europeans but they remain a significant presence along the Gulf of Mexico and the few pockets of Native American communities in the state.</div> </div> </div> </div>This all seems fairly accurate, as an Austin resident myself. There is a small Glass Walker caern in Austin too - drawn in by the promise of a tech boom and all.<br /> <br /> However, I think you forgot one important faction - the Pit(s?) of BSDs that must exist somewhere between Houston, Austin, DFW, and San Antonio whose totem is the Bane Incarna of Traffic...<br /> <br /> Will try to do a write up if Georgia (childhood home) when I get home tonight too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T14:10:31-07:00","id":1297080,"title":"","content":"USA Most Populous Garou Populations by State: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Alabama: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Alaska: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Arizona: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Arkansas: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>California: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Colorado: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Connecticut: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Delaware: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Florida: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Georgia: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Hawaii: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Idaho: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Illinois: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Indiana: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Iowa: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Kansas: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Kentucky: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Louisiana: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Maine: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Maryland: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Massachusetts: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Michigan: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Minnesota: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Mississippi: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Missouri: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Montana: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Nebraska: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Nevada: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>New Hampshire: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>New Jersey: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>New Mexico: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>New York: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>North Carolina: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>North Dakota: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Ohio: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Oklahoma: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Oregon: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Pennsylvania: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Rhode Island: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>South Carolina: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>South Dakota: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Tennessee: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Texas: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Utah: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Vermont: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Virginia: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Washington: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>West Virginia: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Wisconsin: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Wyoming: Bone Gnawer</li> </ol><br /> <br /> If there is one advantage to having low standards and a tribal totem that likes &quot;irresponsible breeding&quot;, it is that you'll end up with a lot of mutts. And that isn't including the fact that they'll take in the riff-raff from basically all the other tribes... Now, if you're talking about tribal representation at Caerns, that's an entirely different story. I suspect that a not insignificant portion of these packs are going to effectively be Road Warriors, and unwelcome at certain caerns.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23808-phoenix","name":"Phoenix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T19:15:42-07:00","id":1297125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1296721-most-populous-tribe-by-state?p=1296936#post1296936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not USA, but I figure if anyone want to involve Finland in the mix, having uusimaa statted out could help.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always figured that there would be at least a small smattering of Silver Fangs, probably of House Crescent Moon, given Russia's proximity and habit of trying to meddle. <br /> <br /> Also that the Uktena would've taken advantage of the post-WW2/Winter War chaos to try to move in among the Sami peoples, much to the annoyance of the Fennoscandian Get of Fenris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T21:30:19-07:00","id":1297148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1296721-most-populous-tribe-by-state?p=1297125#post1297125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always figured that there would be at least a small smattering of Silver Fangs, probably of House Crescent Moon, given Russia's proximity and habit of trying to meddle.<br /> <br /> Also that the Uktena would've taken advantage of the post-WW2/Winter War chaos to try to move in among the Sami peoples, much to the annoyance of the Fennoscandian Get of Fenris.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutely. But I focused mainly on the capital city of Helsinki and the surrounding areas.<br /> <br /> Map here: <a href=\"https://fi.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uudenmaan_maakunta#/media/File:Uusimaa.sijainti.suomi.2011.svg\" target=\"_blank\">https://fi.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uudenm...suomi.2011.svg</a><br /> <br /> Where one might find Fangs would be Kotka (closest to Russia), Vaasa (the old OLD capital) or Turku (the old Capital.) Uktena and Wendigo would be found far far up, in Rovaniemi and above. Sure, some might appear in Helsinki, but not in any greater numbers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T12:04:43-07:00","id":1297552,"title":"","content":"Rage Across Finland is one of those things I keep hoping might show up in the ST's Vault at some point. <br /> <br /> Since I mentioned Alaska, I'm going to guess a relatively large population of Wendigo and Red Talons. Silver Fangs possibly dating back to Russian colonization. Some Bone Gnawers, Fianna and Get of Fenris from the Gold Rush period. A small number of Glass Walkers centered in Anchorage, and a smattering of other tribes. Corax along the coast, a relatively noteworthy population of Gurahl and Qualmi, and various Ratkin lurking about. Maybe a Kitsune visitor or two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T17:11:30-07:00","id":1307058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phoenix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1296721-most-populous-tribe-by-state?p=1297080#post1297080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">USA Most Populous Garou Populations by State:<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Alabama: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Alaska: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Arizona: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>Arkansas: Bone Gnawer</li> <li>California: Bone Gnawer<br /> ...</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>This might not be wrong, but it's not particularly interesting. After the bone gnawers, who do you think would be the next most populous tribes in your home state?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T01:36:16-07:00","id":1307177,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Italy:</b></u><br /> <br /> <b><u>Southern Italy</u>:</b> black furies as natives, Silver Fangs of ancient ancestry or of norman and langobard ancestry, glass walkers and some shadow lords of albanian ancestry from medieval times. Shadow Lords and Glass walkers will probably struggle with the vampires for power among mafia families. <br /> Genetically, southern europe is really mediterranean but it's also the place where, in every century, immigrants from africa and middle east arrived. Silent Striders should be a thing, also because during the 17th century, a lot of gipsyes roamed the lands.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Central Italy</b>:</u> mostly Glass Walkers in rome, Red Talons across the Appennini, some silver fangs from medieval ancestry. Tuscany should be an interesting territory with some of the most ancient feuds between silver fangs tribes, probably enforced by get of fenris. Tuscany is the most ''germanized'' region during the dark ages along with the north. Florence suburban area should be bone gnawer territory. <br /> <br /> <b><u>Northern Italy</u></b>: this should be a Fianna stronghold in the western part and veneto ( the stereotype of venetian people is also the same as the fianna: separatists, loudy, bad temperament and really fierce of their traditions and heritage), with powerful population of Get of Fenris and Silver Fangs from the Ostrogothic and Lombard Kingdom. Shadow Lords should be strong in veneto and friuli, thanks to the story that venice shared for hundreds years with eastern europe. A lot of surnames and slangs come from slavic and dalmatian culture.<br /> Glass and Bone of course in places like Milan, Turin and Padova<br /> <br /> some Cities:<br /> <br /> Milan: almost every tribe should be present in Milan, probably the Glass Walkers would rule the tribal political situation. Even Stargazers and Silent Striders should be here,at least in the city. Outside Milan, Fianna and Get of Fenris would rule the countryside.<br /> <br /> Vicenza: called 'Cymbria' till medieval times after the germanic invasion, that should be a Get of Fenris zone without questions. This is one of the most famous stronghold of the langobards and the all the arheological sites around the citites are currently under examination to preserve the langobardic and gothic artistic heritage of this place. <br /> <br /> Taranto: the most in-famous city because of a giant amiantus power plant. This city should host a huge Hive of Black Spiral dancers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 04-23-2019, 04:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T23:15:25-07:00","id":1307695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1296721-most-populous-tribe-by-state?p=1307058#post1307058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This might not be wrong, but it's not particularly interesting. After the bone gnawers, who do you think would be the next most populous tribes in your home state?</div> </div> </div> </div>Alabama would, at my guess, primarily Fianna and Uktena, with a fair mix of Furies, CoG, Get, Lords, and Striders scattered about, and Glass Walker groups in Birmingham an Mobile (and individual ones in other areas).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T13:24:22-07:00","id":1307830,"title":"","content":"About Spain:<br /> <br /> According the supplements and the novels of tribe:<br /> <br /> -The most populated tribes in the iberian peninsule by historic background are:<br /> <br /> -The Fianna in the West, with the celtic influenced peoples.<br /> -The Bone Gnawers in the East, in the iberian peoples. They celebrated a conclave in Barcelona and in Madrid they are in the powerful caern of the Monasterio de las Trece Penas.<br /> <br /> -Other tribes:<br /> <br /> -Spain has a big population of wolves, with their subspecie. There are a big population of Red Talons.<br /> <br /> -The Children of Gaia have a powerful caern in Castilla, they were present in the moorish kingdoms.<br /> -The Silent Striders arrived too with the moors and invaders of the North of Africa.<br /> <br /> -The Fenrir arrived with the germanic invaders (suevians, vandals and visigoths).<br /> -The Shadow Lords traveled to the New World with the conquerors. It's possible that they have bonds with the spanish nobility. There are presence of the Houses of the Silver Fangs too.<br /> <br /> -It's possible the presence of another tribes as the Black Furies and the Glass Walkers, arrived through the commerce with the Mediterranean Sea.<br /> <br /> -It's possible the presence of american tribes throught the global migration, perhaps Uktena with the migration of South America to Spain.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-26T11:56:03-07:00","id":1308082,"title":"","content":"I want to say that the original Werewolf: The Dark Ages mentioned that the Shadow Lords used the Reconquista to strongly establish themselves in Spain, or at least gave that impression. I may be misremembering though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-28T12:38:45-07:00","id":1314994,"title":"","content":"Michigan: To be fair, I think we have quite the smattering of almost all the tribes. Most populous though? Get of Fenris, Wendigo, Bone Gnawer, Glass Walker. But I'll throw in my thoughts of each tribe.<br /> <br /> Black Furies: I'm sure there's plenty of people with Greek ancestry here, but I'm not aware of any area in the state that is really known for it. Of course Furies could also include those in wome's rights movements, so that could account for some of their numbers here.<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers: Between Detroit, Flint, Saginaw we have more than our share of Gnawers. Throw in Grand Rapids, Lansing, and maybe even some that live on their own outside the cities in the rural north.<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia: Ancestrally not many, but as far as those that have been accepted by this tribe via nature conservancy puts Michigan on the map for Children of Gaia.<br /> <br /> Fianna: UK and Ireland have some representation here. No famous communities of them here, but they're around. The U.P. (Upper Peninsula) had a notable amount of Cornish immigrants back in the mid-late 1800's for the mining industry.<br /> <br /> Get of Fenris: One of our biggest tribes. Much of Michigan was settled by German immigrants. Along with a large population in the U.P. of Finnish descendants that came for mining jobs.<br /> <br /> Glass Walkers: What city doesn't have it's share of Glass Walkers? Don't forget the numerous universities here in Michigan focusing on technology.<br /> <br /> Red Talons: Smaller in numbers, but there is a live wolf population in Michigan, mostly in the north, but there have been some sightings below the Straits of Mackinac. It wouldn't surprise me if the Talons had something to do with our growing wolf population.<br /> <br /> Shadow Lords: Eurasia doesn't have much of a showing here in Michigan, I'm sure there are some. However, outside of politics or any other shady deals, I don't see many Shadow Lords being here.<br /> <br /> Silent Striders: Middle Eastern immigrants have been on the rise here, with the city of Dearborn being made up of mostly those of Middle Eastern descent now. You can't tell me there aren't any Striders among us here.<br /> <br /> Silver Fangs: Similar with the Shadow Lords. Not a strong Russian representation here in Michigan. Are there some? Sure, but they're definitely few and far between.<br /> <br /> Uktena: I always picture Uktena to be more from Central and South America, so not a strong presence here in Michigan. Although many Latinos have come this way working construction jobs.<br /> <br /> Wendigo: Michigan has the largest Native American population east of the Mississippi. Though perhaps overlooked, Wendigo of the Anishinaabe are certainly not to be forgotten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4674-ammayhem","name":"AMmayhem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4674_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-28T18:46:59-07:00","id":1315062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AMmayhem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1296721-most-populous-tribe-by-state?p=1314994#post1314994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uktena: I always picture Uktena to be more from Central and South America, so not a strong presence here in Michigan. Although many Latinos have come this way working construction jobs.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, the general spread was that the Uktena tended to be the tribes and nations from Southeastern and Southwest US and parts further south, while the Wendigo tended to be the Northeast, Great Plains, and Pacific Northwest and further north. The Croatan were coastal MidAtlantic, Ohio/Mississippi River Valleys and a few other places. (There were a few notable exceptions, such as the Apache and Navajo/Dine being Wendigo.) But because of where they were in the Deep South and Mexican regions, and because they didn't share the Wendigo's ideas about racial purity, African American and Mestizo peoples became a fairly sizable part of the Uktena's Kin/breeding stock by the early 19th century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T00:27:25-07:00","id":1315111,"title":"","content":"Uktena were never from South America because there have never been wolves in South America. And the range of the Mexican Wolf in Central America was limited to parts of northern Mexico. There were likely never any Uktena among the Aztecs or Maya. But probably lots of Balam there. And Nuwisha. Lots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-03T08:44:57-07:00","id":1316255,"title":"","content":"Yeah, when it comes to Uktena, Croatan, and Wendigo, I always seem to have a harder time getting a grasp of their origins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4674-ammayhem","name":"AMmayhem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4674_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T12:56:58-07:00","id":1317659,"title":"","content":"I currently live in Texas and used to run a Texas game. Uktena and Fenrir were the big tribes in the state. Also had a bat changer in the game.<br /> <br /> I grew up in Florida. Based on that state's bloody Seminole Wars, I'd say there are a bunch of Weidigo running around. Florida was a big railroad area in the 1800s, so a fair amount of Iron Riders turned Glasswalker.<br /> <br /> Most immigrants in Florida came from South America/Caribbean, so lots of Fera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}